          "status": "permitted"
        },
        {
          "id": "solid-masonry-two-wythe",
          "status": "permitted",
          "note": "The largest estate and hotel work -- Vizcaya, Ca' d'Zan."
        }
      ],
      "rule": "Wood frame carrying an applied stucco skin is the ordinary case; the wall's thickness is read, not structural, except at the grandest estate scale.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "note": "Overrides the inherited continental-baroque-neoclassical masonry-and-terracotta answer, which is Italian Renaissance Revival's American-office construction logic, not this warmer, more vernacular style's own.",
